==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|LL|[[posse]] [[comitātūs]]||force of the county|lit=power of the county}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[able-bodied]] [[men]] over 15 in a given county who can be summoned by the [[sheriff]] to help [[keep]] the [[peace]], or [[arrest]] a [[felon]]; also a group of men so gathered. {{defdate|from early 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1849|author={{w|Henry David Thoreau}}|title=Resistance to Civil Government
|passage=They are the standing army, and the militia, jailers, constables, '''''posse comitatus''''', etc.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Any band of men, especially armed or hostile.
#* '''1819''', Lord Byron, ''Don Juan'', I:
#*: With him retired his ‘'''posse comitatus''',’ / The attorney last, who linger'd near the door / Reluctantly {{...}}

